/*****************************************************************************
    jitJ5 -- RUNG 5 OF THE jitLadder. 2026-07-31.
    J4 + a MULTI-STATEMENT BODY WITH OPERAND REUSE.

    ⚠ THIS RUNG'S PURPOSE IS ATTRIBUTION, NOT COVERAGE. It is the first one
    written to settle a question rather than to extend the surface.

    THE QUESTION: `jitDataClobber` -- jitEmitBinary and jitEmitCompare both end
    by writing the RESULT back onto the TARGET operand's stored SSA value, so a
    node compared once holds an i1 afterward and compared again would be
    `icmp i1, i32`. It has been INFERRED for a month. Rung J3 removed its only
    alleged symptom (testWhilE's ICmp abort, whose real cause was the ungated
    loop executing at emit time), leaving the mechanism UNIMPLICATED: it exists
    in source, acquitted of that symptom, never tested directly.

    THIS IS THE DIRECT TEST. The body reuses ONE FIELD in several roles across
    several statements, and the condition compares a field the body also writes:

        while jeN > 0;
            jeSum = jeSum + jeN;      <- jeN read as an operand
            jeN   = jeN - 1;          <- jeN read AND written, same statement

    jeN is compared (cond), read twice and written once (body), every iteration.
    If a node can hold only one SSA value and the compare's i1 clobbers it, this
    is where it shows -- as an abort, a verifier refusal, or a wrong sum.

        fire 1   jeN = 4  ->  jeSum = 10   (4+3+2+1)
        fire 2   jeN = 5  ->  jeSum = 15   (5+4+3+2+1), NO RECOMPILE

    DIAGNOSTIC VALUES, per rung style:
        10 / 15   correct
         0 / 0    the body never ran
         4 / 5    the loop ran once
        any abort or verifier refusal IS the clobber, and DUMP=2 attributes it

    ⚠ WHICHEVER WAY IT GOES, AN INFERENCE THAT SURVIVED A MONTH IS REPLACED BY A
    READING. Green means the clobber does not bite operand reuse and its scope
    shrinks to whatever is left. Red means it finally has a fixture that can
    attribute it, with DUMP=2 to name the instruction.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (standing harness rule H2).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(JitLadder5);
define
    jeN;
    jeSum;
    jitJ5 code={
        while jeN > 0;
            jeSum = jeSum + jeN;
            jeN = jeN - 1;
        };
    ;

jeN   = 4;
jeSum = 0;
print "J5 fire 1 setup : jeN =" jeN " jeSum =" jeSum:;
testing(jitJ5);
print "J5 fire 1 result: jeSum =" jeSum " (want 10 = 4+3+2+1)":;

jeN   = 5;
jeSum = 0;
print "J5 fire 2 setup : jeN =" jeN " jeSum =" jeSum " (recompile: NONE)":;
jitRefire();
print "J5 fire 2 result: jeSum =" jeSum " (want 15 = 5+4+3+2+1; 0 = body never ran)":;

jeN   = 4;
jeSum = 0;
jitJ5();
print "J5 interpreted  : jeSum =" jeSum " (the oracle -- want 10)":;

print "J5 SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
